<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.841 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.841 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.6 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due May 1, 1997 was 2.841 percent, up from 2.801 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.4 billion of 182-day T-bills due July 31, 1997 was 3.159 percent, up from 3.078 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 357-day T-bills due January 22, 1998 was 3.590 percent, up from 3.495 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$500 million three-month, C$150 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$850 million of C$6.45 billion bills due on Feb 6. (Details follow)  </p>
